partners;
(l)
"Schedule" means the Schedule to this Act;
(m)
"Senate", in relation to any Institute, means the Senate thereof;
(n)
"Statutes" and "Ordinances", in relation to any Institute, mean the Statutes and Ordinances of the Institute made under
this Act.
Chapter II
The Institutes

31.
Statutes.
- Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Statutes may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:-
(a)
the formation of departments of teaching;
(b)
the institution of fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, medals and prizes;
(c)
the terms of office and the method of appointment of officers of the Institute;
